---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../../../data/site.json';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Get Involved & Contribute | Crystal Studio Labs"
  description="Learn how to contribute to Crystal Studio Labs: RFC process, pull request standards, coordinated vulnerability disclosures, and community discussions."
  currentPath="/get-involved/"
>
  <div class="involvement-page">
    <div class="container">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="breadcrumb-nav" aria-label="Breadcrumb navigation">
        <ol class="breadcrumb-list">
          <li><a href="/" class="crumb-link">ROOT</a></li>
          <li class="crumb-separator">/</li>
          <li class="crumb-current" aria-current="page">GET_INVOLVED</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <!-- Page Header -->
      <header class="page-header brutalist-card">
        <div class="hud-corner hud-corner-tl"></div>
        <div class="hud-corner hud-corner-tr"></div>
        <div class="hud-corner hud-corner-bl"></div>
        <div class="hud-corner hud-corner-br"></div>

        <div class="section-marker">// 03 OPEN_SOURCE_COLLABORATION</div>
        <h1 class="page-headline">GET INVOLVED</h1>
        <p class="page-lead">
          We welcome contributions from engineers, Linux system administrators, security researchers, 
          and developers who share our dedication to minimal overhead, rigorous testing, and transparent architectures.
        </p>

        <div class="quick-conduits-row">
          <a href={`${site.github}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary">
            <span>GITHUB DISCUSSIONS</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a href={`${site.github}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-secondary">
            <span>BROWSE OPEN ISSUES</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="btn btn-secondary">
            <span>SECURITY ADVISORY</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">✉</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="involvement-grid">
        <!-- Main Column -->
        <div class="involvement-main">
          <!-- Contribution Workflow -->
          <section class="brutalist-card section-card">
            <div class="section-marker">// WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL</div>
            <h2 class="subhead">HOW TO CONTRIBUTE</h2>
            <div class="steps-list">
              <div class="step-item">
                <div class="step-badge">STEP_01</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                  <h3 class="step-title">Select or File an Issue</h3>
                  <p class="step-desc">
                    Browse open issues across the <a href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link">Crystal Studio Labs GitHub organization</a>. 
                    Before beginning work on major features or architectural refactors, file an issue to confirm alignment with maintainers.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="step-item">
                <div class="step-badge">STEP_02</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                  <h3 class="step-title">Fork & Branch with Conventional Naming</h3>
                  <p class="step-desc">
                    Fork the targeted repository and create a dedicated topic branch:
                    <code>feat/feature-name</code>, <code>fix/issue-description</code>, or <code>docs/update-guide</code>.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="step-item">
                <div class="step-badge">STEP_03</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                  <h3 class="step-title">Enforce Invariants & Run Tests</h3>
                  <p class="step-desc">
                    Ensure your pull request maintains the sub-25MB memory budget, introduces zero native build dependencies (no node-gyp), 
                    and passes all automated unit and smoke tests.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="step-item">
                <div class="step-badge">STEP_04</div>
                <div class="step-content">
                  <h3 class="step-title">Open Pull Request with Conventional Commits</h3>
                  <p class="step-desc">
                    Submit your pull request formatted with Conventional Commits (<code>feat:</code>, <code>fix:</code>, <code>refactor:</code>, <code>docs:</code>, <code>test:</code>). 
                    Include test output and benchmark evidence in the PR description.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- 4-Stage RFC Framework -->
          <section class="brutalist-card section-card">
            <div class="section-marker">// GOVERNANCE_SPECIFICATION</div>
            <h2 class="subhead">4-STAGE RFC LIFECYCLE</h2>
            <p class="section-p">
              Substantial architectural changes, new protocol specs, or repository additions follow our Request for Comments (RFC) process:
            </p>

            <div class="rfc-stages-grid">
              <div class="rfc-box">
                <div class="rfc-tag rfc-draft">STAGE 0: DRAFT PROPOSAL</div>
                <p class="rfc-text">
                  Initial motivation and problem statement submitted as a GitHub Discussion thread. Gathers early feedback on necessity.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="rfc-box">
                <div class="rfc-tag rfc-debate">STAGE 1: COMMUNITY DEBATE</div>
                <p class="rfc-text">
                  Maintainers and community evaluate cross-platform ergonomics, backward compatibility, and alternative approaches.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="rfc-box">
                <div class="rfc-tag rfc-audit">STAGE 2: INVARIANT AUDIT</div>
                <p class="rfc-text">
                  Strict verification of memory ceilings (&lt;25MB), offline viability, license suitability, and dependency footprints.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="rfc-box">
                <div class="rfc-tag rfc-ship">STAGE 3: SHIPPED & MERGED</div>
                <p class="rfc-text">
                  RFC is approved, implementation pull request is merged to <code>main</code>, and changes are tagged with an atomic SemVer release.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Vulnerability Disclosure -->
          <section class="brutalist-card section-card">
            <div class="section-marker">// SECURITY_POLICY</div>
            <h2 class="subhead">COORDINATED VULNERABILITY DISCLOSURE</h2>
            <p class="section-p">
              We take security disclosures seriously. If you identify a security vulnerability, buffer overflow, 
              denial-of-service vector, or token leakage in any Crystal Studio Labs repository, please follow our coordinated disclosure policy:
            </p>

            <div class="security-card">
              <div class="security-row">
                <span class="sec-label">PRIMARY DISCLOSURE EMAIL:</span>
                <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="sec-val">{site.email}</a>
              </div>
              <div class="security-row">
                <span class="sec-label">INITIAL RESPONSE SLA:</span>
                <span class="sec-val">&lt; 24 Hours Acknowledgment</span>
              </div>
              <div class="security-row">
                <span class="sec-label">PATCH DEPLOYMENT SLA:</span>
                <span class="sec-val">&lt; 72 Hours for Critical Advisories</span>
              </div>
              <div class="security-row">
                <span class="sec-label">SAFE HARBOR:</span>
                <span class="sec-val">Full protection for ethical researchers reporting in good faith</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>

        <!-- Sidebar -->
        <aside class="involvement-sidebar">
          <div class="brutalist-card sidebar-box">
            <div class="section-marker">// CODE_OF_CONDUCT</div>
            <h3 class="sidebar-head">COMMUNITY STANDARDS</h3>
            <p class="sidebar-p">
              We enforce the <strong>Contributor Covenant v2.1</strong> across all organization discussions, 
              pull requests, and issue trackers.
            </p>
            <p class="sidebar-p">
              We are committed to providing a welcoming, harassment-free environment for everyone, 
              regardless of experience, background, or identity.
            </p>
            <a href={`${site.github}/.github/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="conduct-link">
              READ FULL CODE OF CONDUCT ↗
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="brutalist-card sidebar-box">
            <div class="section-marker">// COMMUNICATIONS</div>
            <h3 class="sidebar-head">CHANNELS</h3>
            <ul class="channels-list">
              <li>
                <a href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="channel-link">
                  <span class="ch-icon">◈</span>
                  <span>GitHub Organization</span>
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href={`${site.github}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="channel-link">
                  <span class="ch-icon">💬</span>
                  <span>Discussions & RFCs</span>
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="channel-link">
                  <span class="ch-icon">✉</span>
                  <span>Direct Maintainer Contact</span>
                </a>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .involvement-page {
    padding: 2.5rem 0 5rem;
  }

  /* Breadcrumb */
  .breadcrumb-nav {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb-list {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    list-style: none;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .crumb-link {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .crumb-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  .crumb-separator {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .crumb-current {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* Header Card */
  .page-header {
    padding: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    background-color: var(--bg-surface);
  }

  .page-headline {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .page-lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .quick-conduits-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* Grid Layout */
  .involvement-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .involvement-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px;
    }
  }

  .involvement-main {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .section-card {
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .subhead {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .section-p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .text-link {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* Steps List */
  .steps-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .step-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    padding-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .step-item {
      flex-direction: row;
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }
  }

  .step-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .step-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--accent-cyan);
    padding: 0.35rem 0.65rem;
    height: fit-content;
    white-space: nowrap;
    background-color: var(--accent-cyan-dim);
  }

  .step-title {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .step-desc {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .step-desc code {
    background-color: var(--bg-surface-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  /* RFC Stages */
  .rfc-stages-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .rfc-stages-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .rfc-box {
    border: 1.5px solid var(--border-color);
    background-color: var(--bg-surface-elevated);
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .rfc-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .rfc-draft { color: var(--accent-cyan); }
  .rfc-debate { color: var(--accent-amber); }
  .rfc-audit { color: #a855f7; }
  .rfc-ship { color: var(--accent-green); }

  .rfc-text {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Security Card */
  .security-card {
    border: 2px solid var(--border-color);
    background-color: var(--bg-surface-elevated);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  .security-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .security-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .sec-label {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .sec-val {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .sec-val a, a.sec-val {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  /* Sidebar */
  .involvement-sidebar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .sidebar-box {
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .sidebar-head {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .sidebar-p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .conduct-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .conduct-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .channels-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .channel-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    background-color: var(--bg-surface-elevated);
    transition: all 0.15s ease;
  }

  .channel-link:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent-cyan);
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    transform: translateX(2px);
  }

  .ch-icon {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }
</style>
